    "intro_html":  "Lu rou fan is the dish Taiwan runs on. Diced pork braised slowly in soy sauce, caramelized sugar and five spice until it turns glossy and falls apart, ladled over rice with a braised egg on top. Street vendors sell it for pocket change and it deserves the reputation. Our version uses pork shoulder instead of belly, which cuts the fat and pushes it to {{protein}} grams of protein for about ${{cost_ps}} a serving (at everyday cost).",
